                <pb facs="0581" n="457" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg457"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.003/632: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Ruddock</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-07-30T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 30, 1921—3
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>214. Your 256, July 12, noon.</p>
                <p>You may join representatives of other Treaty Powers in accepting proposal for a
                    conference to consider a revision of tariff schedules. Such revised tariff would
                    have eventually to be incorporated in a convention and submitted to the Senate
                    for ratification.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
